  "positiveReview": [
    "The raw all-history fatal UTF-8 audit and 32 MiB cap remain in the workflow. The helper separately uses a 32 MiB aggregate stdout budget, 10,000 commits and bounded subprocess times; it does not truncate or omit ordinary merges.",
    "Single-parent exact literal-path raw diffs preserve A/D/M/T events. Existing add-only validation can still reject edits, deletions, mode changes and re-addition. Independent chmod and rename/deletion fixtures confirm visibility.",
    "For the graph currently supplied by Git, every nonempty merge parent tuple must match result mode/type/blob; merge-created authority, deletion, mode/type changes and conflicting parent authority are rejected. Independent third-parent mutation fixture rejects when not grafted.",
    "Ordinary AA/MM/MA real merges, both parent orders, unchanged authority inherited from one or multiple parents, and three-parent merges pass existing real Git fixtures.",
    "Independent fixed-SHA execution at main7f and PR167 b583 returns exactly the same two binding A events at 286ac82609861e9cf460f69cd0b93ad03724716b and one Receipt A at ae63be23a29a7d4ba8b84c28ff6846cc7318238c; graph sizes 31/34 and merge counts 11/13."
  ],
